{title: The Anchor Holds}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G] I have [C]journeyed
[G] Through the long, dark ni[C]ght[G][D]
Out [Em]on the open s[D]ea
[Am] By faith al[D]one
[G]     [D]Sight un[Em]known
[C]  And yet His [D]eyes were watching [G]me[C/D]

{comment: Chorus}
The anchor [G]holds[C/G][G]
Though the ship is [C]battered[F/C][C]
The an[G/B]chor    [D]holds
Though the sails are [G]torn[C/G][G]
I have [G]fallen [Gmaj7]on my    [G7]knees
As I [C]faced the [G/B]raging  [Am]seas
The anchor [D]holds
In spite of the [G]storm[C/D]

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]  I've had [C]visions
[G]  I've had [C]dreams[G][D]
I've even [Em]held them in [D]my hand
[Am]  But I never [D]knew
[G]  They would [D]slip right [Em]through
[C]  Like they were [D]only grains of [G]sand[C/D]

{comment: Bridge}
[C]  I have been young
[G]  But I am older now
[Em]  And there has been beauty
That these eyes have [D]seen
[C]But it was in the night
[G]  Through the [D]storms of my [Em]life
[C]  Oh, thats where God [D]proved
His love to [G]me[C/D]

{comment: Outro}
I have [G]fallen [Gmaj7]on my    [G7]knees
As I [C]faced the [G/B]raging  [Am]seas
The anchor [D]holds
